All this putting quotes or other markers around deliberately deviant words is s 
little like puttin "[sic]" after every word in Unca' Remus.  It doesn't just 
miss the point, it kills it dead away.  Presumably, the word for "ephalant" is  
'xatno' and if you are of the "heffalump" school, maybe even 'taxno' or 'naxto', 
assuming they are not taken  -- as they aren't.  I would hope that a three year 
old (well, maybe a little older) Lojbanist would get it.


